<section class="eg-page-hero"><div class="eg-container"><div class="eg-breadcrumb"><a href="/ezgraph/workflows/">Workflow examples</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>QuoteGraph</div><span class="eg-eyebrow">The flagship guided conversation</span><h1>Let the model understand.<br>Let your code decide.</h1><p class="eg-lede">QuoteGraph turns a customer's details into a calculated insurance quote. Models recognize information and handle ambiguity. Code validates facts, applies example rating rules, supports revisions, and records acceptance.</p><div class="eg-actions"><a class="eg-button" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/live-replay/">Read the recorded conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="eg-button eg-button-secondary" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/">Explore the complete tutorial</a></div><p class="eg-note">A demonstration application and rating engine. <a href="https://github.com/picoflowio/ezgraph-demo/tree/main/src/graphs/quote-graph">Inspect the source ↗</a></p></div></section>
<section class="eg-section"><div class="eg-container"><div class="eg-section-head"><span class="eg-eyebrow">Five stages. A clear owner for each fact.</span><h2>Follow the application from intake to acceptance.</h2><p>Each stage uses the same prompt, tool, validation, and transition contract. The graph declares business history spaces and a separate termination history.</p></div>
<div class="eg-workflow-row"><span class="eg-workflow-index">01</span><div><h3>Driver</h3><p>Capture identity and license details. Reject invalid dates, unsupported state codes, and inconsistent licensed years before saving the profile.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/validated-tools/">See validated collection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-flow"><strong>capture_driver</strong><span>→</span><strong>VehicleNode</strong></div></div>
<div class="eg-workflow-row"><span class="eg-workflow-index">02</span><div><h3>Vehicle</h3><p>Resolve the customer's vehicle against a code-owned catalog. Ask for disambiguation when several matches remain, then save an accepted selection.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/vehicle-catalog/">See catalog disambiguation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-flow"><strong>resolve_vehicle</strong><span>→</span><strong>capture_vehicle_use</strong></div></div>
<div class="eg-workflow-row"><span class="eg-workflow-index">03</span><div><h3>Insurance history</h3><p>Collect prior coverage and incidents with stage-specific validation. Its business history space keeps detailed incident dialogue separate from general intake.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/sessions-and-history/">See named histories <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-flow"><strong>capture_history</strong><span>→</span><strong>CoverageNode</strong></div></div>
<div class="eg-workflow-row"><span class="eg-workflow-index">04</span><div><h3>Coverage</h3><p>Validate the coverage request against accepted facts. Calculate tiers with a deterministic rating engine, then hand off to presentation.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/deterministic-rating/">See code-owned rating <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-flow"><strong>select_coverage</strong><span>→</span><strong>rateQuote()</strong></div></div>
<div class="eg-workflow-row"><span class="eg-workflow-index">05</span><div><h3>Quote and acceptance</h3><p>Present tiers, apply deductible changes, return to coverage when needed, and record a chosen tier. Code constructs exact confirmation content.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/revise-and-accept/">See revisions and acceptance <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-flow"><strong>adjust_quote</strong><span>→</span><strong>accept_quote</strong></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="eg-section eg-section-tint"><div class="eg-container eg-split"><div><span class="eg-eyebrow">The same contract at each stage</span><h2>Declare what is shared.<br>Keep ownership visible.</h2><p>Driver, vehicle, and coverage nodes share intake history. Insurance incidents and quote presentation use separate business spaces. The graph's model policy and restore policy have established locations alongside topology.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/tutorials/quote-graph/graph-and-state/">Explore the graph and state registry <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="eg-code"><div class="eg-code-head"><span>quote-graph.ts · history excerpt</span><span>TypeScript</span></div><pre><code class="language-typescript">historySpaces: [
  [DriverNode, "quote-intake"],
  [VehicleNode, "quote-intake"],
  [HistoryNode, "quote-incidents"],
  [CoverageNode, "quote-intake"],
  [QuoteNode, "quote-present"],
  [TerminateSessionNode, "quote-terminal"],
]</code></pre></div></div></section>
